      "title": "Australian politics live: Greens condemn rightwing push against social media reform and vow to table bill to block US execution livestream",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/15/anthony-albanese-labor-pauline-hanson-monoculture-victorian-election-coalition-angus-taylor-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Follow the day’s news live.</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Private health insurance changes ‘recalibrating precious taxpayer dollars’, says Wells</strong></p><p>The health minister, <strong>Mark Butler,</strong> yesterday promised to reintroduce a bill to reduce private health insurance rebates for over-65s, after it was thrown out of the Senate by the crossbench and Coalition.</p><p>It’s really important we reintroduce it, because we need to raise the level of support and resourcing for aged care. I was the aged care minister before being the communications minister, we need to work urgently. There’s not enough beds being built for older Australians who need that support. It’s recalibrating precious taxpayer dollars.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/15/anthony-albanese-labor-pauline-hanson-monoculture-victorian-election-coalition-angus-taylor-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-15T02:03:54"
    },
    {
      "title": "Labor and Coalition block bill that would ban incarcerated women being shackled in childbirth",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/15/labor-coalition-bill-banning-shackling-incarcerated-women-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Liberal Paul Scarr breaks ranks to condemn major parties, saying he will write to Queensland attorney general</p><ul><li><p>Follow our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/15/anthony-albanese-labor-pauline-hanson-monoculture-victorian-election-coalition-angus-taylor-ntwnfb\">Australian politics live blog</a> for latest updates</p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Labor and the Coalition have blocked a vote on a bill that would have banned the shackling of incarcerated women during childbirth, with the government saying it was the responsibility of the states and territories.</p><p>Independent senator Lidia Thorpe introduced the bills into the Senate, which would prevent shackling and stop children being strip-searched.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/15/labor-coalition-bill-banning-shackling-incarcerated-women-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-15T00:22:33"
    },
    {
      "title": "As One Nation rises, Victorian Labor has promised to make abortions free. Is the timing pure politics?",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/15/victorian-state-election-labor-pledges-free-abortion-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Facing the prospect of election defeat, Labor is hoping to make abortion a defining issue as the Liberals attempt to stave off claims they would oversee a rollback</p><ul><li><p>Follow our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/oct/15/anthony-albanese-labor-pauline-hanson-monoculture-victorian-election-coalition-angus-taylor-ntwnfb\">Australian politics live blog</a> for latest updates</p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Victorian Labor’s plan to make abortion free has been years in the making. But make no mistake: the timing of the announcement is pure politics.</p><p>On Thursday morning, the state’s health minister, Ingrid Stitt, announced if re-elected in November, Labor would invest $30m over four years to remove the out-of-pocket cost of abortion care, which can quickly add up to more than $1,000.</p><p>Benita Kolovos is Guardian Australia’s Victorian state correspondent</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/15/victorian-state-election-labor-pledges-free-abortion-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-15T00:17:18"
    },
    {
      "title": "Illegal tobacco increasingly hard to spot, with some fakes in plain packaging featuring Australian health warnings",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/15/black-market-tobacco-fakes-australian-health-warning",
      "description": "<p>Government warned that counterfeit tobacco produced by criminal organisations in south-east Asia is becoming more sophisticated</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The black-market tobacco trade continues to thrive as sellers turn to counterfeit packaging to skirt bans, prompting calls for the urgent passing of tougher laws.</p><p>Intelligence provided to the federal government shows cigarettes in plain Australian-style packaging are being produced illegally at an industrial scale in south-east Asian warehouses.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/15/black-market-tobacco-fakes-australian-health-warning\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-14T23:32:14"
    },
