      "description": "<p>Federal authorities issued more than a dozen grand jury subpoenas in inquiry into potential immigration fraud</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/oct/14/donald-trump-us-midterms-arizona-montana-politics-latest-news-updates\">US politics live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Federal authorities investigating the Minnesota representative <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ilhan-omar\">Ilhan Omar</a> seized the Democratic lawmaker’s phone and have issued more than a dozen grand jury subpoenas, including to some of her relatives, according to a person briefed on the inquiry.</p><p>The subpoenas were issued for a grand jury collecting evidence in <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/minnesota\">Minnesota</a> as federal authorities investigate potential fraud in Omar’s immigration paperwork, said the person, who spoke on the condition of anonymity because they were not authorized to discuss an ongoing investigation. The investigation led to federal agents searching Omar’s Washington DC home on Monday just weeks before the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-midterm-elections-2026\">November midterms</a>, in which Omar is seeking re-election.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/14/ilhan-omar-phone-seized-relatives-subpoenaed\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
